{
  "id": "u02-l02",
  "unit": "u02-pronouns",
  "title": "We & they",
  "status": "draft",
  "tip": "Add **-রা** (*-ra*) to make pronouns plural:\n\n- আমি → **আমরা** (*amra*) we\n- তুমি → **তোমরা** (*tomra*), আপনি → **আপনারা** (*apnara*) you all\n- সে → **তারা** (*tara*), ও → **ওরা** (*ora*) they (polite: **ওনারা** *onara*)\n\nGood news: **the verb does not change for plural.** আমি ভালো **আছি**, আমরা ভালো **আছি**. আপনি **আছেন**, আপনারা **আছেন**. The ending only cares about *person* and *respect*.\n\nNouns usually don't need a plural ending when the context is clear: **তারা ডাক্তার** = 'They are doctors.' And **ছেলে / মেয়ে** mean 'boy / girl' but also 'son / daughter' — you'll use that in the Family unit.",
